            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>L-Carnitine is a key regulatory compound of glucose and fatty acid metabolism in the myocardium. A number of experimental observations indicate that L-Carnitine may favorably influence the outcome of the myocardium after ischemic injury.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
